retty and  bright and the music's gorgeous and  everything seems happy and childish but  there are really really dark undertones  the painting feature is actually pretty  amazing the fact that you can sort of  small for yourself onto a wall and then  view an environment entirely differently  and be able to search it out or find a  way over  in a way that you wouldn't have been  able to before is really really  appealing it sort of makes you think of  the game in three separate ways you've  got the huh I don't know how to get past  this this environment has some kind of  stone that I can't lift what do I do  then there's the painting aspect and  then there's the items aspect which is  general in all these other games one  major changes that this game definitely  doesn't hold your hand a lot of people  complained about Skyward Sword being too  easy or telling you what to do in this  game doesn't do that it marks a red X on  your map it doesn't tell you how to  actually get to that red X you could go  up the top of the map the side of them  at the bottom of the map approach from  all these different angles and try and  get there and they'll be obstacles in  your way and you don't know which way is  the definite way to cook I got a little  bit frustrated with that but not  actually because of the game just  because of me  sometimes I got pretty lost I'm really  bad at Zelda games actually perhaps my  only annoyance with the game is when  it's loading all you have to say walk  across the screen you're walking right  to left and then when you get to the  left there's a little breeze before it  loads the other side it doesn't just  follow a link in the center it has to  load different areas so yeah you'll walk  one side to the other and in the freeze  it is what gets me it's a noticeable  pause and I don't know for some reason  that really bothered me all in all it's  a really really beautiful addition to  the Legend of Zelda franchise and I  really hope we see more of yog